<lines>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_1">>>>82 Etiam legale pretium auget affectio.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_2">>>>83 Tertia causa augendi pretium est prae¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_3">>>stantia mercis.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_4">>>>84 Sicut etiam deterior merces minuit</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_5">>>pretium.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_6">>>>85 Quarta causa est periculum non</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_7">>>soluendi in vendente.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_8">>>>86 Quinta causa periculum non soluen¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_9">>>di mercem in emente.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_10">>>>87 Obijcitur, &amp; soluitur.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_11">>>>88 Certum est periculum hoc esse pretio</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_12">>>aestimabile.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_13">>>>89 Cautè taxandum periculum, &amp; parui.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_14">>>>90 Sexta causa augendi est asportatio</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_15">>>ad alium locum.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_16">>>>91 Duobus modis potest intelligi.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_17">>>>92 Res hic existens quomodo possit ven¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_18">>>di pretio existentis alibi</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_19">>>>93 Is qui merces aliò erat translaturus</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_20">>>illius loci pretio potest vendere,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_21">>>&amp; pretium hic augere.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_22">>>>94 Emptores lanarum minoris multis</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_23">>>titulis excusantur.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_24">>>>95 Septima causa pretium augendi est</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_25">>>donatio liberalis.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_26">>>>96 Certum est veram donationem non</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_27">>>solùm minuere, sed omnino tol¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_28">>>lere pretium.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_29">>>>97 Donationem pretium minuere Do¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_30">>>ctores asserunt.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_31">>>>98 Quando vis, aut dolus intercedit do¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_32">>>natio non praesumitur.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_33">>>>99 Ignorantia donationem excludit.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_34">>>>100 Amici consanguinei, &amp; sodales prae¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_35">>>sumuntur donare.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_36">>>>101 Octaua causa est modus vendendi</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_37">>>explicandus.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_38">¶DIximus quae pretium ordinarium,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_39">&amp; currens in rep. non tam augent,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_40">quam constituunt; quia cum semper cum</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_41">pretio communi coniuncta sint, com¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_42">mune pretium non variatur ex illis, sed</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_43">ex illis consurgit, quod ideo naturale</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_44">vocatur: in taxa verò, quia semper in¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_45">terueniunt, semper sunt attendenda,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_46">sicut in pretio etiam conuentionali, at¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_47">que adeo hoc etiam pretium consti¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_48">tuunt, si iustè definiantur. ////Dicamus iam de</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_49">ijs, quae pretijs ordinarijs accidunt, vt il¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_50">la vel augeant vel minuant, non semper, sed</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_51">quando eueniunt. ////Quę disceptatio ad tol¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_52">lendas hinc fraudes, &amp; scrupulos valde</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_53">vtilis est. ////Sunt ergo aliqua, quae pretium</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_54">vulgare, &amp; ordinarium in rep. constitu¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_55">tum, siue legale, siue naturale augendo,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_56">vel minuendo variant.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_57">¶//Primum est damnum emergens, vel</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_58">lucrum cessans duo fulmina belli scho¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_59">larum, seu vt melius dicam, duo vasa</line>
</lines>
